# Wren's cottage, Act I.
# The supper plays when the hero comes home through the door with the kindling.

== supper ==
[background cottage_hearth]

The fire is lit. Honey cakes are cooling on the table, and Ash is already under it.
WREN (happy): There you are! And kindling too. Set it by the hearth, love.

# Dying to the wisp on the errand sets died_on_errand (the first Underreach trip).
[if died_on_errand] WREN (worried): You're white as milk. What happened out there?
[if died_on_errand] * truth: "There was a wisp. Then everything went grey."
[if died_on_errand] * fib: "Nothing. I tripped in the dark."
[if picked truth] WREN (afraid): ...Grey.
[if picked truth] WREN (worried): Sit down. Eat something. You're home now.
[if picked fib] WREN (sad): Mm. You never could lie to me, you know.
[if not died_on_errand] HERO: Ash spotted a wisp in the trees. We gave it a wide berth.
[if not died_on_errand] WREN: Good lad. Good lads, both of you.

WREN (happy): Eighteen. I can hardly credit it.
WREN: I've kept something for you since you were small enough to sleep in the bread basket.
She sets a bundle of oilcloth in front of you. Inside is a plain knife with a worn horn handle.
WREN (sad): It was your father's.
[give fathers_knife]

* thanks: "Thank you, Gran. I'll look after it."
* father: "What was he like?" [set asked_about_father]
[if picked thanks] WREN (happy): See that it looks after you.
[if picked father] WREN (happy): Stubborn. Kind to dogs and fools. You've got his hands.
[if picked father] WREN (sad): ...Eat your cake.

Her eyes go to the door. It's the third time tonight.
* door: "Are you expecting someone?" [set asked_about_door]
[if heart >= 2] * scared: "You're frightened, Gran. Tell me why." [set pressed_wren]
* Say nothing.
[if picked door] WREN (worried): Expecting? No. No one comes out this far after dark.
[if picked scared] WREN (sad): Some nights are older than others, that's all. Humour an old woman.

HERO: Ash doesn't look a day older than when I was little. How old is he now?
WREN (happy): More cake?

Ash pads over to the door and whines to be let out.
* Let Ash out.
* "He wants out, Gran."
WREN (afraid): No!
WREN (worried): ...Not tonight. He can go out in the morning.
She drops the heavy bar across the door. Ash lies down against it, facing out.
[do bar_door]
WREN (happy): There. Snug as a hearth-cat. Happy birthday, {hero}.
[set supper_done]


# Talking to Wren in the cottage, outside the supper.
== wren_chat ==
[if not supper_done] WREN (happy): Kindling before supper, love. Stay in sight of the path.
[if not supper_done] WREN: And take Ash. He knows those trees better than you do.
[if supper_done] WREN (happy): Off to bed with you, birthday boy.


# Looking at the wedding portrait on the cottage wall. It's an object, so it's all narration.
== wedding_portrait ==
Your mother and father on their wedding day, stiff in their best clothes.
A black dog sits at their feet.
# A story event: only after the midpoint revelation at the Drowned Chapel.
[if ledger_read] The paint is cracked with age. It's older than you are.
[if ledger_read] The dog in it hasn't changed at all.
